SUMMARY:Architectural Walking Tour of Yale and Lunch in New Haven NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nRegister by July 10. No refunds. Let's explore the 
 world-famous architecture of Yale University and the quaint college town of 
 New Haven!\n\nGUIDE: Laszlo Kiss\, an internationally known architect and 
 popular Adult School instructor.\n\nSCHEDULE:\n\n\n	7 a.m. Leave 
 Montclair\n	10 a.m. Arrive New Haven\n	10 a.m. - 12:30 P.M. Laszlo will 
 lead us through a tour of Yale's modernist masterpieces by architects such 
 as Louis Kahn\, Eero Saarinen\, Paul Rudolph\, and Gordon Bunshaft of 
 Skidmore\, Owings & Merrill. We’ll also get to view great works of art 
 inside the Yale Center for British Art and the Yale University Art 
 Gallery.\n	12:30-2 p.m. Lunch break. \n	\n		Eat lunch on your own at one of 
 the many cute campus-area eateries (including the famous Sally's Apizza) 
 and browse the charming little shops\, bookstores and coffeehouses near 
 campus. \n		OR Join Laszlo for a 15-minute walk (each way) to the Ingalls 
 Rink\, Yale's modernist hockey arena. You'll still have time to catch a 
 quick bite to eat.\n	\n	\n	2:30 p.m.-3:30 p.m. Meet at Yale Visitors Center 
 for student-led tour of the old campus\, established in 1701\, which is not 
 accessible to solo visitors. This includes the iconic Gothic-style Sterling 
 Memorial Library and the ivy-clad residential campuses.\n	3:30-4 p.m.  
 Browse the Yale University Bookstore before getting back on the bus\n	4:30 
 p.m. Board the bus for Montclair!\n\n\nBRING:  Sunscreen\, comfortable 
 walking shoes\, hat. Dress in layers. \n\nACCESSIBILITY INFORMATION: This 
 is a three-hour walking tour with some uneven ground. Some buildings do not 
 include elevators. \n\nPlease note: Lunch is not included. This trip will 
 be held rain or shine.
LOCATION:Montclair - Offsite\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-16767995
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16767995
END:VEVENT
