X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Cloud Data Driven": "https://www.meetup.com/cloud-data-driven/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_cloud_data_driven
URL:https://www.meetup.com/cloud-data-driven/
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Cloud Data Driven
UID:event_315353906@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260720T040732Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T133000
SUMMARY:MCP Server with Fabric - Meeting Cancelled
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Data Driven\n**We regret to inform you that this event h
 as been cancelled.** We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause\, a
 nd we are currently working to reschedule this session.\n\n🔸 Important!
  **Microsoft Community Tenant is retiring** (Community operations continue
 !)\n\nBeyond this specific cancellation\, we would like to update the Data
  Driven community regarding significant infrastructure changes that might 
 impact our operations.\n\nAs announced by Microsoft\, **the Microsoft Comm
 unity Tenant (msftcommunity.com) is scheduled to be retired** on Thursday\
 , August 6\, 2026. You can read the official announcement from Microsoft h
 ere: [https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/mgci-news/community-and-edu
 cation-tenant-retirement/4528125](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog
 /mgci-news/community-and-education-tenant-retirement/4528125)\n\nThis chan
 ge presents substantial challenges for our community operations\, as our c
 urrent infrastructure - including our Microsoft Teams environment - relies
  on this tenant.\n\nWe are currently evaluating our options and working to
  determine how we can continue our activities in the future. At this time\
 , there is no other change - please follow our website for further announc
 ements.\n\n**🔸 Future Data Driven Summit 2026 is cancelled!**\n\nFurthe
 rmore\, we would like to share that we have made the decision not to run t
 he [Future Data Driven Summit](https://datadrivencommunity.com/FutureDataD
 riven2025.html) this year. After multiple successful years of running what
  is likely the biggest Data platforms virtual event\, with dozens of speak
 ers and thousands of registrants\, we will skip this year and pause our fl
 agship summit as we navigate these changes.\n\n**🔸 Community email and 
 contacting the team**\n\nSince the Microsoft Community Tenant (msftcommuni
 ty.com) will be retired\, all our emails using that domain will no longer 
 work. Should you have any questions or need to reach out to the community 
 team\, please feel free to contact us directly via LinkedIn:\nRonen Ariely
 : [https://www.linkedin.com/in/pitoach](https://www.linkedin.com/in/pitoac
 h)\nJean Joseph: [https://www.linkedin.com/in/jeandjoseph](https://www.lin
 kedin.com/in/jeandjoseph)\nDeepthi Goguri: [https://www.linkedin.com/in/de
 epthigoguri](https://www.linkedin.com/in/deepthigoguri)\n\nOr use our new 
 community public email address:\n[contact@datadrivencommunity.com](contact
 @datadrivencommunity.com)\n\n🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹
 🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹🔹\n[Original Event Details and Abstract below]\n\nI
 n this session\, I explore how the Model Context Protocol (MCP) enables a 
 new way for AI agents to securely and intelligently interact with Microsof
 t Fabric.\n\nYou’ll see how MCP servers expose Power BI semantic models 
 and Fabric data agents as discoverable tools\, allowing agents to reason o
 ver enterprise data\, query it in natural language\, act on top of it and 
 edit semantic models for Power BI.\n\nI will walk through real scenarios w
 here data agents and Power BI models become first-class citizens in agent 
 workflows\, unlocking more contextual\, trustworthy\, and scalable AI expe
 riences across the Fabric ecosystem.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/cloud-data-driven/events/315353906/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260621T140747Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260621T140747Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
