SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] World of Film with Mark Phelan
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nGentlemen Prefer Blondes (1953) | 
 NR\nLorelei Lee is a beautiful showgirl engaged to be married to the 
 wealthy Gus Esmond\, much to the disapproval of Gus' rich father\, Esmond 
 Sr.\, who thinks that Lorelei is just after his money. When Lorelei goes on 
 a cruise accompanied only by her best friend\, Dorothy Shaw\, Esmond Sr. 
 hires Ernie Malone\, a private detective\, to follow her and report any 
 questionable behavior that would disqualify her from the marriage.\n\nABOUT 
 THE INSTRUCTOR\nMARK PHELAN - I am a lifelong film fanatic who eats\, 
 breathes\, sleeps and drinks movies. I have studied with Donald Spoto at 
 the New School in NYC and have a BA and MA in Speech and Theatre from MSU. 
 I have also worked as an actor and have directed several plays in local 
 regional and community theaters\, including the Whole Theatre in Montclair 
 and the Paper Mill Playhouse in Millburn\, NJ. I am currently working as an 
 adjunct professor teaching\, among other courses\, Introduction to 
 Cinema.\n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis class is run by the MILL. Please register 
 for classes directly through their website here.\n\nFor questions about 
 MILL classes please call 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is made possible 
 through a partnership between the MILL\, Montclair Public Library and 
 Partners for Health.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Books, Film & Theater
UID:LibCal-10306-16678848
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16678848
END:VEVENT
