SUMMARY:Spec-Driven Performance
DESCRIPTION:NJ Code & Coffee\nNJ Code and Coffee presents a talk on "Spec-
 driven Development: Using spec-driven development for production workflows
 ".\n\nAI coding assistants excel at small tasks and isolated features. But
  when you're building something that spans multiple files and requires upf
 ront planning\, they fall apart.\n\nSpec-driven development fixes this. Wr
 ite the spec first\, let the AI build from it\, then iterate.\nThis talk b
 reaks down how to do it in three phases\, what tradeoffs you'll hit\, and 
 how to start using it\nin your next feature.\n\n\\*This talk is a part of 
 NJ Code & Coffee's regular monthly meetup.\n**Doors open at 2pm\, talk sta
 rts at 3\, arrive early for networking and light refreshments.**\nBring yo
 ur laptop.\n\n**The Speaker**\n[Erik Hanchett](https://www.linkedin.com/in
 /erikhanchett/) is a developer who creates technical content\, build apps\
 , and speak at events around the world about frontend\, JavaScript\, AI\, 
 and the future of modern development. A lot of what he enjoys most is help
 ing developers connect new ideas to real-world software they’re actually
  building.\n\n**You MUST register for the event in order to get into the b
 uilding.**\nJoin the NJ Code & Coffee Community Discord - come hang out be
 fore and after:\n[www.codeandcoffee.chat](http://www.codeandcoffee.chat/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/nj-code-coffee/events/315660607/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260713T011354Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260713T011354Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
