X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_north_jersey_bowling_soccer_volleyball
X-SOURCE:Meetup: NJ Bowling, Volleyball, Tennis & More
UID:event_315550800@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260720T040734Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260801T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260801T120000
SUMMARY:Weekend Warrior Tennis (Saturdays)
DESCRIPTION:North Jersey Bowling\, Volleyball\, Tennis And More\nWe meet a
 t 9AM unless one or more people comment wanting to meet at 8AM which is my
  preferred time. You’re welcome to show up any time but are encouraged t
 o post it so we have a better idea of what to expect for that day. (Those 
 who share the same comment for start time can simply like that comment so 
 we see how many show up for that time without potentially cluttering the c
 omments.)\n\n**RULES:** By signing up you agree to follow these rules:\n\n
 1\\. No instruction or orders are allowed on any of our group courts\\. If
  two or more people are in agreement then they’re welcome to exchange in
 structions so long as they relinquish their court positions and don’t di
 srupt active players\\. If anyone is instructing or ordering you and you
 ’re not comfortable then please tell them or let me know\\. Everyone sho
 uld feel free to play however they wish without being directed without agr
 eement\\\, most especially beginners\\.\n\n2\\. No formal matches are allo
 wed on any of our group\\-reserved courts\\. If people are in agreement th
 en they’re welcome to find another court not in use by our group to play
  strict matches\\. If we need to rotate people in and out due to lack of e
 nough courts then we’ll follow my Florida instructor’s method for bala
 nced clinic matches\\. This will typically include quick matches to 5 poin
 ts after which everyone rotates clockwise one position\\. This keeps those
  waiting rotated back in often and also discourages team clotting\\.\n\n3\
 \. We are foremost beginner\\-friendly and not aggressively competitive or
  an instruction\\-oriented group\\. A little light and friendly competitio
 n or giving a quick tip so long as you’re not holding up the court is OK
  but please pace yourself against the person you’re hitting to \\(e\\.g\
 \. hit softer to members that might not be as good or as aggressive as you
 \\)\\. Everyone should be made to feel welcome and free regardless of skil
 l level\\. Beginners most especially should always feel comfortable here\\
 .\n\n4\\. Please make sure you’re signed up using a name that matches yo
 ur Meetup name\\. New players should always check in with me so I can mark
  you down as having checked in\\. Anyone showing up without a Meetup RSVP 
 will be asked to do so before they can participate in the event\\. If you
 ’re bringing one guest that’s fine\\\, just make sure to mark them on 
 your RSVP\\.\n\n5\\. If I feel you’re consistently not following the rul
 es I have the right to ask you to relinquish your position on the court\\.
  Please don’t sign up and attend if you don’t agree to following any o
 ne rule here\\. We are largely democratic but I reserve the right to make 
 any final calls if I deem it necessary for any reason\\\, such as breaking
  up and remixing long\\-locked groups if we have more than one court\\.\n\
 n**EQUIPMENT:** Please bring your own racquet and water\, as we don’t pr
 ovide those. I always have some balls for at least one court\, but feel fr
 ee to bring your own in case we need to branch out over more than one cour
 t.\n\n**DISCLAIMER:** Courts are subject to availability and weather. If y
 ou make plans to attend please be prepared to cancel or adjust our locatio
 n as needed. Furthermore\, by attending you agree to be fully responsible 
 for your own health and safety. Each person is responsible to take a break
  for rest and water at their own discretion.
