SUMMARY:Jewelry Making Bootcamp
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nJoin us for three fast and furious afternoons of jewelry 
 making basics. We'll look at commercially made findings and how they work\, 
 and then we'll make our own. We'll see what makes a design wearable or 
 not\, and how to make a good design even better. Tools\, beads\, wire and 
 lots more come under scrutiny. This class is for beginners and those who 
 want to push their jewelry work into new realms. The more you make\, the 
 more you'll learn\, so expect homework. Students must purchase 
 approximately $30 of materials to bring to the first class: round nose 
 pliers\, chain nose pliers\, flush or semi-flush cutter\, 20-gauge wire and 
 a handful of beads.\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Arts & Crafts
UID:LibCal-10306-16878287
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16878287
END:VEVENT
