SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] World of Film with Mark Phelan
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nThe Ghost and Mrs. Muir (1947) | 
 NR\nDefying her conventional in-laws\, young widow Lucy Muir leaves London 
 with her young daughter and moves away for a quieter life in a secluded 
 seaside cottage. Lucy discovers the ghost of the deceased former owner\, 
 sea captain Daniel Gregg\, is haunting the house\, but gathers the courage 
 to stand up to him\, and woman and ghost become friends. Faced with 
 dwindling means of support\, Lucy agrees to the Captain's challenge to 
 write his colorful life story.\n\nABOUT THE INSTRUCTOR\nMARK PHELAN - I am 
 a lifelong film fanatic who eats\, breathes\, sleeps and drinks movies. I 
 have studied with Donald Spoto at the New School in NYC and have a BA and 
 MA in Speech and Theatre from MSU. I have also worked as an actor and have 
 directed several plays in local regional and community theaters\, including 
 the Whole Theatre in Montclair and the Paper Mill Playhouse in Millburn\, 
 NJ. I am currently working as an adjunct professor teaching\, among other 
 courses\, Introduction to Cinema.\n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis class is run by 
 the MILL. Please register for classes directly through their website here. 
 This class is offered both in-person and hybrid on Zoom.\n\nFor questions 
 about MILL classes please call 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is made possible 
 through a partnership between the MILL\, Montclair Public Library and 
 Partners for Health.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Books, Film & Theater
UID:LibCal-10306-16678850
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16678850
END:VEVENT
