SUMMARY:Selichot - Service\, Dinner\, Music!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T213000
DTSTAMP:20260716T031014Z
UID:TU2131910341
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T181500
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Events
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260714T210247Z
DESCRIPTION:Welcome in the spirit of the High Holidays with a participator
 y\, music-filled night! Connect with the Shomrei community over dinner\, s
 ing High Holiday melodies\, and have some fun at our jazz dessert receptio
 n.\n\n**RSVP Required for Dinner and Reception** https://www.google.com/ur
 l?q=http://shomrei.org/jazz&sa=D&source=calendar&ust=1781360942935189&usg=
 AOvVaw2KtNcG4NBtMMqfUMMmuO3K\n\nFree or Suggested Donation:  \n$20 per adu
 lt\, $10 per child over 12\, $36 per family\n\n**-------------------------
 -----  \nAdults and Kids 8+ (Younger Kids/Scroll Down)**  \n6:15 - 7:15pm\
 , Dinner  \nEnjoy a Chicken Schwarma\, middle eastern dinner (vegan option
 s available and pasta options for kids) in the Social Hall.  \nrsvp requir
 ed  \n  \n7:15 - 7:30pm\, Havdalah  \nAs Shabbat comes to a close\, childr
 en and adults will come together to recite Havdalah prayers. We are lookin
 g forward to having our children who are 8 yrs old and up help lead the ha
 vdalah candle lighting ceremony while reciting prayers with Rabbi Julie.\n
 \n7:30 - 8:30pm\, Musical Selichot Service (Zamru-Style!)  \nParticipatory
 \, music-filled service led by Rabbi Julie\, Talia Lakritz\, Suzanna Grobm
 an\, Debra Caplan and accompanied by Oren Neiman and his jazz ensemble.\n\
 nSelichot_Booklet: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://drive.google.com/f
 ile/d/1CfQz_30MYWaFAZKkGfbE57su_JTd1D1O/view?usp%3Ddrive_link&sa=D&source=
 calendar&ust=1781360942935189&usg=AOvVaw3LFD9NLsOy19_F5ZK2IKI-  \nStreamin
 g: https://www.google.com/url?q=http://shomrei.org/live&sa=D&source=calend
 ar&ust=1781360942935189&usg=AOvVaw0X3JDM7-oYxg01_V5kqhOz\n\n  \n8:30 - 9:3
 0pm\, Dessert &amp\; Jazz Reception  \nThe party continues with a dessert 
 reception. Live music will be provided by the jazz ensemble. We will also 
 ask participants to interact with our Selichot art installation by adding 
 your thoughts and wishes to our interactive board.\n\n**------------------
 ------------**\n\n**Kids 7 and Younger**  \n6:15 - 7:15pm\, Little Kid's D
 inner &amp\; Hangout (play time)  \n(in the YAC)  \nrsvp required  \n  \n7
 :15 - 7:30pm\, Havdalah  \nAs Shabbat comes to a close\, children and adul
 ts will come together to sing the Havdalah blessings. We are looking forwa
 rd to having our children who are 8 yrs old and up lead the havdalah candl
 e lighting ceremony while reciting prayers with Rabbi Julie.  \n  \n7:30 -
  8:45pm\, Little Kid's Movie &amp\; Selichot Art Project  \nDrop off the l
 ittle kids\, childcare is free. (in classroom 1 &amp\; 2) Children are wel
 come to make art to add to our interactive Selichot art installation.\n\n 
  \n8:45 - 9:30pm\, Childcare  \nDrop off the little kids\, childcare is fr
 ee. (in the YAC)  \n **------------------------------**\n\n**Have question
 s? Want to Help out? Contact:** Shomrei Office  \noffice@shomrei.org  \n(9
 73) 746-5031\n\n**What is Selichot?**  \nThe Hebrew word selichah means 
 “forgiveness.” The plural form of the word selichah is selichot\, a wo
 rd traditionally used to refer to additional prayers for forgiveness recit
 ed during the month of Elul (through Yom Kippur). We gather together on th
 e Saturday night before Rosh Hashanah to meditate on the capacity for forg
 iveness and on its power. In joining together we help each other pray for 
 that blessing – to give it and to receive it.\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260715T170352Z
LOCATION:Social Hall\, Gallery\, [#]holiday:rosh_hashanah
TRANSP:OPAQUE
