SUMMARY:New Jersey Symphony: Handel’s Messiah
DESCRIPTION:Run Time: 2 hours and 15 minutes \nNew Jersey Symphony’s glorious holiday tradition returns with this iconic masterpiece\, a classical rendition of the greatest story ever told\, composed by George Frideric Handel and featuring the Montclair State University Singers. The majestic music—including the triumphant “Hallelujah Chorus”—rekindles the spirit of the holidays for first-time listeners and those who return each season. \nThis event features composer Kendrick Armstrong\, soprano Jessica Rivera\, mezzo-soprano Kelley O’Connor\, tenor Martin Bakari\, and bass-baritone Adam Lau. The MSU Singers are directed by Heather J. Buchanan.
URL:https://www.peakperfs.org/event/new-jersey-symphony-handels-messiah/
CATEGORIES:2026 - 2027
